{"chunk_id": "eeb58b9ad226", "text": "Arjuna asks the fire\u2011god Agni (Pavaka) for proper weapons, steeds, and a radiant chariot so he and Krishna can help him burn the vast Khandava forest despite Indra\u2019s attempts to stop the blaze. Agni summons Varuna, lord of waters, who provides divine armaments: the legendary bow Gandiva, two inexhaustible quivers, and a magnificent ape\u2011bannered chariot for Arjuna, along with celestial horses. Krishna receives a returning discus and the thunderous mace Kaumodaki. Armed with these gifts, the two heroes declare themselves ready to confront even gods and demons if necessary. Empowered by their pledge, Agni expands into his fierce form and engulfs the Khandava forest in flames, roaring like storm clouds and blazing like the sun upon Mount Meru. The passage marks the arming of Arjuna and Krishna with iconic weapons and the dramatic beginning of the Khandava conflagration.\nVaruna grants Arjuna the Gandiva bow, inexhaustible quivers, and a celestial chariot, while Krishna receives the discus and mace before Agni begins burning Khandava forest.\nThemes: divine weapons, Krishna and Arjuna alliance, divine intervention, prelude to Khandava burning, cosmic warfare", "vector": [0.003759230487048626, -0.010385212488472462, -0.011433199048042297, 0.024529654532670975, -0.01072327233850956, 0.03294059634208679, -0.034806687384843826, -0.004394783638417721, -0.025476224720478058, -0.016308028250932693, 0.014563637785613537, 0.012021424248814583, 0.020554065704345703, 0.0036442899145185947, -0.0005383610259741545, 0.016470298171043396, 0.03602370619773865, -0.001573670655488968, 0.019593974575400352, -0.01601053588092327, -0.011264168657362461, 0.006578653585165739, -0.005256837699562311, 0.009560344740748405, -0.009769942611455917, 0.03037133626639843, 0.007897088304162025, -0.022825831547379494, 0.0012913902755826712, -0.000701475131791085, -0.009479210712015629, 0.005703077185899019, 0.00341778970323503, -0.0008552925428375602,